derekt75 wrote:
>
> agreed: you should be okay as long as you're not fighting too many
> soldiers at once.  Keep in mind @s don't respect Elbereth, so don't
> rely on that as an emergency plan when surrounded by soldiers.  Don't
> get drowned by an eel.  You can use a polearm to kill the eels and
> also to kill Croesus from across the moat (although it'll take a lot
> longer than going in with Firebrand).

If you find a bear trap in the mines and you can get to the second door
fast enough, apply the bear trap towards/into the doorway.  Then each
soldier will be trapped as they try to move throw the doorway to attack
you.  Then stand back and hit ech of them with a polearm.  Classes who
can advance the polearm skill can exercise it enough at that doorway to
be offered to #enhance it, sometimes even to skilled.

Having skilled in polearm lets you hit on a knights move.  That doesn't
matter with eels in the moot but it's nice to be able to attack Croesus
indirectly across the moat.

Having skill in polearm is nice at the Castle to hit monsters as they
come out to attack you.  This works best if you can destroy the
drawbridge so they stand in the gate square but can't cross the moat. 
Then use boulders from a giant or from the sokoban scrolls to fill the
moat after the Castel crowd has thinnned.


